B.FT=s(["The lanterns leaned east together, as if pointing along an old path.","A second tide showed the same lean \u2014 a route, not a coincidence."],t.s)
B.Do=new A.c8("driftmoor_lantern_route","driftmoor","The Drifting Lantern Route","Where do the reef lanterns go when the tide turns?","Watch which way the lanterns lean at low water and note the route they seem to remember.",B.fI,B.FT,"The lantern route runs toward Sunreed. Someone there once trimmed these wicks.","sunreed_lantern_wicks","sunreed","The Lantern Reef keeps a drifting route east, toward the reed fields.","Water casks in the hold caught the lantern light and showed the same eastward lean.")
B.EC=s(["Only a northern wind woke the bells, in a slow falling scale.","The scale repeated at dusk, lined up with the far spire."],t.s)
B.Dp=new A.c8("sunreed_reed_bells","sunreed","Reed-Bell Alignment","Why do the reeds chime only when the wind comes from the spire?","Listen for the small bells tied among the reeds and note which winds wake them.",B.d4,B.EC,"The reed bells are tuned to Farhaven. Their echo must land somewhere high in the cloud.","farhaven_listening_chamber","farhaven","The Golden Reed Fields chime in a scale aligned with Farhaven Spire.","Silk strung between the reeds carried the chime farther than the wind alone.")
B.Ev=s(["Pale leaves curl open wherever the cloud touches the stone.","Seed pods drift loose on the evening updraft, falling toward the sea."],t.s)
B.Dv=new A.c8("farhaven_cloudline_garden","farhaven","The Cloudline Garden","What grows on the ledges where the cloud ceiling rests?","Look along the high ledges for plants that live on mist alone.",B.d5,B.Ev,"The cloudline seeds fall toward Driftmoor. The shoals may be catching them.","driftmoor_tidal_seedbeds","driftmoor","The Cloudline Spire seeds its mist garden downward, toward the shoals.","Herbs from the hold drew the mist-leaves open a little wider on the ledge.")
B.EH=s(["A shed wall is hung with braided wick, the same weave as the reef.","An old cutter remembers setting lanterns afloat for lost skiffs."],t.s)
B.Dn=new A.c8("sunreed_lantern_wicks","sunreed","Lantern Wicks in the Reeds","Who trimmed the wicks that drifted to Driftmoor?","Search the reed-cutters' sheds for the same braided wick the reef lanterns carry.",B.fJ,B.EH,"The lanterns were a kindness: a route home, set adrift from Sunreed. The first wick, the cutters say, was lit from a lamp at Moonwake Observatory.",null,"moonwake","Sunreed cutters once sent lanterns to the shoals to guide skiffs home.","The cutters knew the spice at once \u2014 they used to braid it into wicks to keep them burning.")
B.EP=s(["A hollow landing hums faintly whenever the north wind blows.","Carved star marks ring the chamber, matching the bells' scale."],t.s)
B.Dm=new A.c8("farhaven_listening_chamber","farhaven","The Listening Chamber","Where in the spire does the reed-bell echo land?","Follow the faint chime upward through the spire's quiet stairwells.",B.d6,B.EP,"The chamber is an old sky clock, kept in time by the reeds below \u2014 and its echo carries on, toward a ring of glass.","glassward_hollow_song","glassward","Farhaven hides a listening chamber that keeps time with Sunreed bells.","Star charts laid on the chamber floor lined up exactly with the carved marks.")
B.Ff=s(["Pale shoots cling to an old hull plate half-buried in sand.","The shoots have spread into a small, mist-loving meadow."],t.s)
B.Dr=new A.c8("driftmoor_tidal_seedbeds","driftmoor","Tidal Seedbeds","Do the cloudline seeds take root in salt water?","Wade the shallow beds at low tide and look for pale leaves.",B.fG,B.Ff,"A garden from the spire now grows in the shoals, tended by the tide. At night its leaves lean toward a dome in the sky.","moonwake_dawn_garden","moonwake","Driftmoor shallows hold a tidal garden grown from Farhaven seeds.","A spare hull plate gave the young shoots a second place to cling.")
B.EI=s(["The lens holds a faint green glow just above the Driftmoor horizon.","The glow rises every night over the shoals, never over open sky."],t.s)
B.Dt=new A.c8("moonwake_night_lens","moonwake","The Night Lens","What was the great lens watching when its keepers left?","Wait for full dark and look through the old brass lens without moving it.",B.fH,B.EI,"The keepers were not watching stars. They were watching something grow \u2014 and left seeds for the dome to do the same.","moonwake_dawn_garden","moonwake","Moonwake's night lens was aimed at a green glow over the shoals.","A compass set beside the lens settled on the same bearing as the green glow.")
B.ER=s(["Pale mist-leaves have sprouted along the dome gutters overnight.","At dawn the leaves turn to follow the fading moon, just like the lens."],t.s)
B.Dq=new A.c8("moonwake_dawn_garden","moonwake","The Dawn Garden","Can a mist garden grow on a roof that faces the moon?","Climb to the dome at first light, where dew gathers in its gutters.",B.d5,B.ER,"The garden keeps the observatory's hours: open all night, folded shut at sunrise.",null,null,"Moonwake's dome carries a garden that follows the moon until dawn.","Herbs tucked into the gutters gave the new leaves something to lean toward.")
B.F6=s(["Each gallery answers a little later than the last, like a slow round.","A hush in one doorway puts the whole ring out of step."],t.s)
B.Du=new A.c8("glassward_echo_galleries","glassward","The Echo Galleries","Why does every glass shard answer a sound a moment late?","Walk the ring's galleries and clap once in each, counting the delay.",B.d4,B.F6,"The galleries are one instrument, waiting around the ring for a single true note.","glassward_hollow_song","glassward","Glassward's galleries echo in sequence, one instrument around a ring.","Silk hung in a doorway softened the echoes enough to count them clearly.")
B.Fb=s(["A low note from the north makes the nearest shards glow.","At dusk the whole ring sings the reed-bell scale back toward Sunreed."],t.s)
B.Ds=new A.c8("glassward_hollow_song","glassward","The Hollow Song","What note do the reed bells and the glass ring share?","Stand at the heart of the ring when the north wind blows and listen for the note that reaches every shard.",B.eh,B.Fb,"Cloudhaven's islands are tuned to one another: reeds, spire, and glass sing a single song.",null,null,"Glassward Halo answers the reed bells, carrying one song across the skyway.","A gem held up at the ring's heart split the song into bright, separate colors.")
